From de756776d931c05fc6ff4cf3aa70ca54027b1c36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:24:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] testsuite: microblaze: fix the isa tests and the LTO
 scans

Every gcc.target/microblaze test that fails on microblaze-elf fails for
a reason in the testsuite, not the compiler:

- isa/fcmp1.c to fcmp4.c, nofcmp.c and vanilla.c call print without
  declaring it, an error since GCC 14.  Declare it.
- isa/fcmp4.c expects "f1 == f2" as fcmp.eq.  GCC now branches around
  the call on fcmp.ne, which is just as correct; fcmp3.c already
  accepts either.
- microblaze.exp sets TORTURE_OPTIONS itself, so gcc-dg.exp does not set
  gcc_set_required_options to -ffat-lto-objects, and every scan-assembler
  test in others/ fails under -flto -fuse-linker-plugin
  -fno-fat-lto-objects, which leaves no assembly to scan.  Set it after
  loading gcc-dg.exp.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/microblaze/microblaze.exp: Set
	gcc_set_required_options to -ffat-lto-objects.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp1.c: Declare print.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp2.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp3.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/isa/nofcmp.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/isa/vanilla.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp4.c: Likewise.  Accept fcmp.ne
	as well as fcmp.eq.
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp1.c    | 2 ++
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp2.c    | 2 ++
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp3.c    | 2 ++
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp4.c    | 4 +++-
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/nofcmp.c   | 2 ++
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/vanilla.c  | 2 ++
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/microblaze.exp | 7 +++++++
 7 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp1.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/microblaze/isa/fcmp1.c
